-- Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA), 07-a0-00, Part III Division 3 (Retaliatory action taken by lessor):
-- ss 26A and 26B, inserted by the Residential Tenancies Amendment Act 2024 s 17 (in operation 16 May 2024).
-- Source: sources/rta-1987.07-a0-00.mrdoc_49316.txt lines 555-582. Reference register REF-03, REF-12
-- (encoded here), REF-13, REF-16 to REF-21 (facts), REF-14, REF-15, REF-22 (the in-scope links).
-- LQA step 4A, 4 October 2026. Not yet through 6H.

IMPORT `part-1-definitions`

§ `Section 26A -- Retaliatory action`

-- The kinds of action s 26A(a) lists, and others. Which action the lessor took is a fact; an increase
-- of rent "under the residential tenancy agreement" is one made by notice under s 30 or s 31A (REF-14);
-- action to terminate includes a notice under s 64 or s 70A (REF-15) and any other (REF-16).
DECLARE `Action by the lessor` IS ONE OF
    `a notice claiming a breach, other than a failure to pay rent, and requiring it to be remedied`
    `a notice claiming a failure to pay rent`
    `an increase of the rent payable under the agreement`
    `a higher rent under a further agreement with the tenant`
    `action to terminate the agreement`
    `a refusal, at the end of the current agreement, to enter into a further agreement with the tenant`
    `some other action`

-- s 26B(2)(a)-(c): the matters after which an action may be retaliatory.
DECLARE `Matter in s 26B(2)` IS ONE OF
    `the tenant or a representative entity took action to enforce the tenant's rights (s 26B(2)(a))`
    `the lessor or its agent knows of a complaint about the lessor to the Commissioner or another government entity (s 26B(2)(b))`
    `an order of a competent court is in force in relation to the lessor and tenant (s 26B(2)(c))`
    `none of those matters`

-- The facts of an alleged retaliation (REF-17 to REF-21).
DECLARE `Alleged retaliation` HAS
    `matter`                                                        IS A `Matter in s 26B(2)`
    `the matter arose on`                                           IS A NUMBER
    `action`                                                        IS AN `Action by the lessor`
    `the action was taken on`                                       IS A NUMBER
    `the lessor was motivated, wholly or partly, by the matter arising` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the tenant reasonably believes the action was retaliatory`     IS A BOOLEAN

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 26A, "a matter referred to in section 26B(2)(a), (b) or (c)"
GIVEN m IS A `Matter in s 26B(2)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 26A -- is a matter referred to in s 26B(2)(a), (b) or (c)` m IF
    NOT (m EQUALS `none of those matters`)

-- s 26A(a)(i)-(iv). FK-11, reading taken (A): "increases the rent payable under the residential tenancy
-- agreement" is an increase of the rent under the agreement the tenant holds; a higher rent fixed by a
-- further agreement is not within (ii), and offering one is not a refusal within (iv).
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 26A(a)(i)-(iv); fork FK-11 reading A
GIVEN x IS AN `Action by the lessor`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 26A(a) -- is an action listed` x IF
        "(i)"   ... x EQUALS `a notice claiming a breach, other than a failure to pay rent, and requiring it to be remedied`
    ..  "(ii)"  ... x EQUALS `an increase of the rent payable under the agreement`
    ..  "(iii)" ... x EQUALS `action to terminate the agreement`
    OR  "(iv)"  ... x EQUALS `a refusal, at the end of the current agreement, to enter into a further agreement with the tenant`

-- FK-11, reading rejected (B): a higher rent fixed by a further agreement with the tenant is an
-- increase of the rent within (ii).
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 26A(a)(ii); fork FK-11 reading B
GIVEN x IS AN `Action by the lessor`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `FK-11 reading B -- s 26A(a) -- is an action listed` x IF
        `s 26A(a) -- is an action listed` x
    OR  x EQUALS `a higher rent under a further agreement with the tenant`

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 26A(a), (b)
GIVEN r IS AN `Alleged retaliation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 26A -- the lessor takes retaliatory action` r IF
        `s 26A -- is a matter referred to in s 26B(2)(a), (b) or (c)` (r's `matter`)
    AND "(a) takes any of the following action" ... `s 26A(a) -- is an action listed` (r's `action`)
    AND "(b) is motivated to take the action, wholly or partly, by the matter arising"
    ... r's `the lessor was motivated, wholly or partly, by the matter arising`

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 26A(a), (b); fork FK-11 reading B
GIVEN r IS AN `Alleged retaliation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `FK-11 reading B -- s 26A -- the lessor takes retaliatory action` r IF
        `s 26A -- is a matter referred to in s 26B(2)(a), (b) or (c)` (r's `matter`)
    AND `FK-11 reading B -- s 26A(a) -- is an action listed` (r's `action`)
    AND r's `the lessor was motivated, wholly or partly, by the matter arising`

§ `Section 26B -- Retaliatory action taken by lessor`

-- s 26B(2): "This section applies if a tenant reasonably believes the lessor took retaliatory action
-- against the tenant after any of the following matters arose". The day the matter arose and the day
-- the action was taken are facts; on the same day the order is unknown, and the encoding allows it.
-- What the tenant believes is of retaliatory action, so the action must be one s 26A lists.
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 26B(2)
GIVEN r IS AN `Alleged retaliation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 26B(2) -- the section applies` r IF
        "a tenant reasonably believes the lessor took retaliatory action" ... r's `the tenant reasonably believes the action was retaliatory`
    AND `s 26A(a) -- is an action listed` (r's `action`)
    AND "after any of the following matters arose" ... `s 26A -- is a matter referred to in s 26B(2)(a), (b) or (c)` (r's `matter`)
    AND r's `the action was taken on` AT LEAST r's `the matter arose on`

-- s 26B(3): the tenant may apply to a competent court for relief (REF-19, REF-21).
@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 26B(3)
GIVEN r IS AN `Alleged retaliation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 26B(3) -- the tenant may apply to a competent court for relief` r IF
    `s 26B(2) -- the section applies` r

-- s 26B(4): if the court is satisfied the action was likely to have been retaliatory action for a
-- s 26B(2) matter, it may make any order it considers appropriate, for example setting the action
-- aside, or compensation for loss or injury other than personal injury. Whether the court is
-- satisfied, and what it orders, are facts (REF-21).
DECLARE `Order sought under s 26B(4)` IS ONE OF
    `an order setting aside the lessor's action`
    `compensation for loss or injury other than personal injury`
    `compensation for personal injury`
    `another order the court considers appropriate`

@ref Residential Tenancies Act 1987 (WA) s 26B(4)
GIVEN r IS AN `Alleged retaliation`
      `the court is satisfied the action was likely to have been retaliatory action` IS A BOOLEAN
      o IS AN `Order sought under s 26B(4)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 26B(4) -- the court may make, on the application` r `, satisfied:` `the court is satisfied the action was likely to have been retaliatory action` `, the order` o IF
        `s 26B(3) -- the tenant may apply to a competent court for relief` r
    AND `the court is satisfied the action was likely to have been retaliatory action`
    AND NOT (o EQUALS `compensation for personal injury`)
